# ML Pipeline Template — Production-Ready Machine Learning System

A modular, domain-agnostic ML pipeline. Train on mock data to learn the full ML lifecycle, then adapt to any classification domain.

---

## What Is This?

A complete machine learning system covering data ingestion, preprocessing, feature engineering, model training, evaluation, and inference. Designed for students and developers to learn ML pipelines end-to-end, then fork and adapt to real projects.

### Key Features

- **3-Model Ensemble Classifier** (RandomForest + CatBoost + GradientBoosting) with 5-fold stratified cross-validation
- **~28 Engineered Features** extracted automatically from structured data
- **Three-Model Architecture**: Classifier, priority predictor, and pattern detector
- **Database-Agnostic**: SQLAlchemy backend supports SQLite, PostgreSQL, MySQL, SQL Server — swap connection strings, no code changes
- **Mock Data Generator**: Built-in synthetic data for learning and testing the pipeline end-to-end
- **Production API**: FastAPI server for real-time inference
- **CLI Tools**: Command-line interface for training, evaluation, and analysis

---

## Quick Start (Windows PowerShell)

### Prerequisites

- **Python 3.10+** — Download from [python.org](https://www.python.org/downloads/)
  - During install, check **"Add Python to PATH"**
- **Git** (optional) — Download from [git-scm.com](https://git-scm.com/download/win)

### Clone & Install

Open PowerShell and run:

```powershell
# Clone the repo (or download ZIP and extract)
git clone https://github.com/mansredfire/ml-pipeline-template.git
cd ml-pipeline-template

# Allow scripts to run (one-time)
Set-ExecutionPolicy -ExecutionPolicy RemoteSigned -Scope CurrentUser

# Create and activate virtual environment
python -m venv venv
.\venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1

# Set Python path so imports work
$env:PYTHONPATH = "$(Get-Location)"

# Install dependencies
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

### Verify Installation

```powershell
python -c "from src.collectors import DataRecord; print('Installation successful')"
```

### Train with Mock Data

```powershell
python scripts/train_with_mock_data.py --quick --reports 1000
```

---

## Quick Start (Mac / Linux)

```bash
git clone https://github.com/mansredfire/ml-pipeline-template.git
cd ml-pipeline-template
python3 -m venv venv
source venv/bin/activate
export PYTHONPATH="$(pwd)"
pip install -r requirements.txt
python scripts/train_with_mock_data.py --quick --reports 1000
```

---

## Usage

All commands assume your virtual environment is activated and you're in the project directory.

### Train with Mock Data

```powershell
python scripts/train_with_mock_data.py --quick --reports 1000
```

The mock data generator creates synthetic records with randomized types (10 simple stock event categories), severities, and metadata. This exercises the full pipeline without needing real data.

### Train from Config

```powershell
python scripts/train_model.py --config config/training_config.yaml
```

### Analyze a Target

```powershell
python scripts/analyze_target.py --domain AAPL --tech Bloomberg Refinitiv
```

### Batch Analyze

```powershell
python scripts/batch_analyze.py --input targets.csv --output results.json
```

### Evaluate Models

```powershell
python scripts/evaluate_models.py --models-dir data/models
```

### Run the API Server

```powershell
python app.py
# API at http://localhost:8000
# Docs at http://localhost:8000/docs
```

---

## How the Pipeline Works

```
Mock Data / Your Data
        │
        ▼
   Preprocessing
   (normalize, deduplicate, enrich)
        │
        ▼
   Feature Engineering
   (~28 features extracted per record)
        │
        ▼
   Model Training
   (3-model ensemble + 5-fold cross-validation)
        │
        ▼
   Evaluation
   (accuracy + F1 on held-out test set, CV scores)
        │
        ▼
   Saved Models (.pkl files)
        │
        ▼
   Inference via API or CLI
```

### Three Models

| Model | What It Does | How It Works |
|---|---|---|
| **Classifier** | Predicts event type (like "Stock Goes Up" or "Bad Forecast") | 3-model ensemble: RandomForest, CatBoost, GradientBoosting with 5-fold stratified CV |
| **Priority Predictor** | Predicts severity/priority level | RandomForest with stratified CV and label encoding |
| **Pattern Detector** | Finds multi-step patterns across records | Rule-based pattern matching (no ML) |

### What the Feature Engineer Extracts (~28 features)

Severity score, priority score, reward amount, source quality, auth required, user interaction, complexity flags, HTTP method encoding, tech stack count, description length, risk score, and more. See `src/features/feature_engineer.py` for the full list.

